<title>USA: Lockheed unit gets $56 mln Navy contract.</title>
<headline>Lockheed unit gets $56 mln Navy contract.</headline>
<dateline>NASHUA, N.H. 1997-02-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sanders, a Lockheed Martin Corp subsidiary, said on Wednesday it won a $56 million contract from the U.S. Navy to to continue production of the AN/SRS-1A combat direction-finding systems.</p>
<p>The contract is for seven systems  and three upgrade field kits in the next two years. It includes options for 16 more systems for delivery through 2002 for a total value of $125 million.</p>
<p>((-- New York Newsdesk 212 859-1610))</p>
